message.content:
Cushion covers of linen fall under HTS 6304 (other furnishing articles). Subheading 6304.19 covers bedspreads, and 6304.91 covers other furnishing articles that are knitted or crocheted. 6304.92 covers those not knitted or crocheted, of cotton, and 6304.93 covers those of synthetic fibers. 6304.99 covers those of other textile materials, which includes linen: 6304.99.6000 is "Other: Other" for non-knitted fibers other than cotton. The statistical suffix is 6304.99.6030 or 6304.99.6020, but I am not certain which. I recall 6304.99.6000 as the breakout "Other" with no suffix, so the code would be 6304.99.6000.

However, there may be a question of whether the decorative chain and charms make the item something else, such as a composite good. The textile pillow cover is the essential character, so it stays in 6304. Pillow covers of linen are usually classified in 6304.99.6000, so I'll go with that.

{"hts_code": "6304.99.6000", "reason": "Linen non-knitted decorative pillow cover (cushion cover) with attached decorative chain is an 'other furnishing article' of textile material other than cotton or synthetic fibers, under heading 6304, subheading 6304.99."}
